# gbuild - code ownership
#
# The paths below are the build engine, its enforcement hooks and its
# verification contract. Any change to them is the kind of change that can
# break every project built with this tool, so review is requested from the
# owner of the engine before merging.
#
# NOTE (solo maintainer): this file routes review requests and documents
# ownership. It cannot make GitHub block merges for a single-account
# repository - that needs branch protection with a required reviewer, which
# the maintainer enables in repository settings. The local enforcement lives
# in Hooks/git/pre-push.ps1: a push touching Modules/ is blocked unless an
# attestation exists (GBUILD_REVIEW_APPROVED=<name>, a 'Reviewed-by:' commit
# trailer, or GBUILD_REVIEW_OVERRIDE=<reason> as an explicit recorded waiver).
# CI runs regardless of either gate.

/Modules/              @dvlproeng-02
/Hooks/                @dvlproeng-02
/Steps/                @dvlproeng-02
/.github/workflows/    @dvlproeng-02
/Tests/                @dvlproeng-02
/gbuild.ps1            @dvlproeng-02
/gbuild                @dvlproeng-02
/gbuild.bat            @dvlproeng-02
/gbuild.config.json    @dvlproeng-02
/gbuild.config.schema.json @dvlproeng-02
